      "body": "## Overview\r\n\r\nFixes test_muse_spark_rocm_mono.py failures introduced by the interaction of #62757 (shared RoPE via get_rope()) and #63440 (monokernel).\r\n\r\n## Claims\r\n\r\n- Fixes all 26 test_muse_spark_rocm_mono failures (cos_sin_cache must be a contiguous 2-D CUDA tensor)\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\nTested on MI350X (gfx950) against vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:nightly-76c6f3f2a with both this patch and #65080 hotpatched:\r\n\r\n- Before fix: 26 failed (cos_sin_cache error)\r\n- After fix: 33 passed, 0 failed (29.79s)\r\n\r\n## Details\r\n\r\nget_rope() caches RotaryEmbedding instances globally and may create the cos_sin_cache buffer on CPU. The non-fused RoPE path handles this via _match_cos_sin_cache_dtype(), but the fused HIP kernel and the monokernel access the buffer directly.\r\n\r\nThis patch normalizes the shared cache once at load time in process_weights_after_loading, before maybe_attach_mono, so both the fused kernel and the monokernel see a contiguous CUDA buffer from the start. No forward-path overhead.",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "akii96"
            },
            "body": "Closing as it turns out the CPU cache only leaks from a test, not in production. #65140 + #65080 have it covered. ",
